# Build context exclusions for deploy/lambda_native/Dockerfile.
#
# BuildKit prefers "<dockerfile-path>.dockerignore" over the repository-root
# .dockerignore, so this file scopes the Lambda build without touching the
# upstream LightRAG Docker setup. Nothing listed here is deleted from the
# branch — it is excluded from the image build only.

# Everything is excluded by default; the image needs three paths.
*
!lightrag/**
!emotion_api/**
!deploy/emotion_artifact/split455_train273_case_w1_gemini_1536/**
!deploy/lambda_native/requirements.txt

# Re-exclude what must never enter the image even under the allowed paths.
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.DS_Store
**/*.log

# The packaged WebUI and Swagger assets are static files served by the FastAPI
# app, never imported. Python packages under lightrag/ are all kept: several
# modules import siblings lazily, and pruning them for a few MB would make the
# fork's import graph fragile for no meaningful size win.
lightrag/api/webui/**
lightrag/api/static/**
